  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 210 AM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nThe active pattern looks to continue as we head into early next \nweek, as upper ridging begins to amplify across the western CONUS. \nThis leads to strong and persistent west-northwest flow aloft. \nGuidance suggests more than a few shortwaves will progress through \nthe mean flow aloft, with a near daily threat for showers and \nthunderstorms across the area. PWAT values will also fall into next \nweek, as we lose the monsoonal tap with the transition to northwest \nflow. Some threat for severe storms will also persist into early \nnext week, mainly across western Nebraska.  \n\nTemperatures look to remain near to below average into next week as \nwell, with daily highs in the upper 70s to lower 80s into midweek. \nTuesday looks to be the exception to this, with strong warm \nadvection ahead of an approaching frontal boundary boosting highs \ninto the upper 80s to lower 90s. This will keep any heat \nconcerns away, with a pleasant week expected temperature wise \nacross the area.",
